    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it feels like a huge gamble for someone like me though. if i raise my prices to cover the wages, i might lose customers to big box stores that can afford the hit, but if i dont, i cant pay my staff. when you look at the actual outcomes, does it usually end up being a net positive for small towns, or is it mostly just a way to help workers at the expense of small business owners?",
